    "reasoning": "Nitpicks: (1) The agent briefly executed an accidental combined query (“errorissue”) while transitioning between searches—this is a minor process mistake if the required searches are ultimately completed. (2) Inspecting slightly fewer than 5 results for a term would be acceptable if fewer substantive results exist or if the agent clearly explains limitations.\n\nCritical issues: (1) The agent did not complete the required four searches. Evidence shows a completed search for “error” and later “issue” (and an erroneous “errorissue”), but there is no evidence of any searches for “failed” or “help” and no stated blocker preventing those searches. (2) The agent did not inspect up to 5 most recent substantive results per term across all four terms; most inspection activity is confined to the “error” term and a single “issue” thread. (3) The agent did not deduplicate across terms (and in practice didn’t even generate a multi-term set to deduplicate). (4) The agent did not produce the required final output table with the specified columns; the predicted output is a narrative for one “issue” thread only, not the requested cross-term table.\n\nWhat the agent did accomplish: It correctly opened Slack global search, ran “error”, opened multiple “error” results and some thread replies, then ran “issue” and opened a specific thread. Screenshot 27 strongly supports the contents of the Ding Aug 20 thread and that it is explicitly resolved. Also, there is no evidence the agent modified Slack content (no send/edit/react).\n\nOutcome assessment: From a user perspective, the core deliverable is the consolidated table covering four search terms with up to 5 recent results each, deduplicated, with resolution status. The agent produced only one entry (for “issue”) and did not perform two of the four required searches nor deliver the table. This falls well short of the primary intent, so the task is not successfully completed even though the single reported thread appears accurate and read-only.",
    "verifier_name": "mm_rubric_outcome",
